            <ArticleTitle>Who should be taking aspirin to prevent coronary events?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1076-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The decision to prescribe aspirin to prevent a coronary event is not straightforward, and requires physicians to balance the risk of a coronary event with the risk of adverse events from aspirin. Although evidence-based medicine shows the way, it does not answer all the questions, especially for patients at intermediate risk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
